rs\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system\ndocker compose up --build\n```\nThis builds the multi-stage Docker container and starts both the application and a dedicated PostgreSQL database container.\n\n---\n\n### **Once the System is Running, Use These Endpoints & Accounts:**\n\n| URL | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **[http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080)** | **Public Verification Portal** (Lookup & verify certificates) |\n| **[http://localhost:8080/login](http://localhost:8080/login)** | **Staff Login** |\n| **[http://localhost:8080/dashboard](http://localhost:8080/dashboard)** | **Issuance & Management Dashboard** |\n| **[http://localhost:8080/audit](http://localhost:8080/audit)** | **Immutable Audit Log** |\n| **[http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html](http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html)** | **Interactive REST API Documentation (Swagger)** |\n\n#### **Demo Logins:**\n- **System Admin**: `admin` / `Admin@12345` *(can revoke credentials and view logs)*\n- **Registrar Officer**: `officer` / `Officer@12345` *(can issue new qualifications)*\n\n#### **Sample Certificates to Test in the Search Bar:**\n- **Genuine Certificate**: `QVS-2024-BSC-8891` (Sarah Jenkins)\n- **Revoked Certificate**: `QVS-2022-DIP-1109` (Marcus Vance)\n- **Invalid Certificate**: `TEST-INVALID-99`\n\n---\n\n### **To Run Automated Tests & JaCoCo Coverage:**\n- Double-click **`run-tests.bat`** (or run `.\\run-tests.bat` in terminal).\n- This executes all 26 automated unit and integration tests and outputs the coverage report to:\n  `target\\site\\jacoco\\index.html`","thinking":"The goal is to provide a straightforward method for local project execution. A simple \"one-click\" approach appears feasible for Windows environments. The user needs to locate and execute a specific batch file within the project's directory. This should trigger the project's compilation and startup process within a command prompt window.\n\n\n"}
